# Walkthrough - Neumorphic Sliding Auth Redesign

I have completely pivoted the authentication experience to a **Neumorphic (Soft UI)** aesthetic, implementing a horizontal "Sliding Overlay" for the Login/Register forms.

## Key Implementation Details

### 1. Neumorphic Design System
- **Custom Shadows**: Implemented `shadow-nm-flat` and `shadow-nm-inset` utilities in Tailwind. These create the distinctive and soft "extruded" look in dark mode.
- **Base Background**: Adjusted the background to `#0c0d21` for the perfect soft UI balance.

### 2. Neumorphic Navbar
- A floating, centered navigation bar with tactile buttons.
- **Pressed State**: Buttons appear to physically sink into the navbar on click (`nm-inset` animation).

### 3. Tactile Sliding Auth
- **AuthContainer**: Horizontal sliding overlay with soft shadows.
- **Soft UI Forms**: Redesigned [LoginForm](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/AuthCard.tsx#20-92) and [RegisterForm](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/auth/AuthCard.tsx#93-168) with inset shadows for inputs and raised-surface buttons.

